We compile this C code with `gcc -S -O0 -masm=att -o my_syscall_example.s my_syscall_example.c`.
Using `-O0` (no optimization) ensures that the assembly closely reflects the C code structure, making it easier to follow. `-masm=att` specifies AT&T syntax.

